{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Extend video (Wan2.2 Fun VACE)",
    "description": "Core nodes + Adrift's cj_video_extend nodes (CJColorMatchToReference, CJRetimeFrames). Generation: the source window (whole clip up to 20 s, shorter for heavy resolutions/frame rates) is resampled to 16 fps and squeezed (no crop) onto the ~480p VACE canvas; its last 17 frames are kept as context (mask black) and followed by gray frames VACE fills in (mask white). Output: the source window at its native resolution, frame rate and audio (node 30, only re-encoded by SaveVideo) followed by the continuation, which is colour-matched to the context in LAB (node 50), retimed from 16 fps to the source fps by duplicating/dropping frames (node 56) and lanczos-upscaled to the source size (node 55); silence pads the audio under the continuation. The last 17 generated frames (16 fps, canvas size, before H.264) are also saved as PNGs under video/adrift_ctx/<video name>/ (node 53, hidden from the gallery) so extending this output again conditions on lossless frames. Two-stage Wan2.2 sampling (8 steps, shift 8): high-noise model without LoRA at cfg 3.5 for steps 0-4 (prompt adherence), low-noise model + lightx2v 4-step LoRA at cfg 1 for steps 4-8. speed=fast puts the high-noise LoRA (node 5) in and runs 4 steps at cfg 1 on both stages."
  },
